descriptions.description:
Design, develop, and deploy artificial intelligence solutions and automations to solve business problems and improve operational efficiency;
Develop and maintain scalable AI solutions that are sustainable and secure;
Integrate AI models into existing business systems, applications, and digital platforms;
Collaborate with data engineers and analysts to collect, clean, and prepare data for model development;
Ensure data quality, integrity, and compliance with data governance standards;
Develop feature engineering approaches to enhance model performance;
Perform ongoing model tuning, optimisation, and retraining to ensure effectiveness over time;
Troubleshoot and resolve technical issues related to AI models and deployments;
Execute small projects or key tasks in larger projects;
Coordinate cross-functional stakeholders, including technical teams, business units, and vendors;
Conduct testing, validation, and quality assurance prior to implementation;
Maintain project documentation, technical specifications, and implementation records;
Identify opportunities to leverage AI to improve processes, automate workflows, and enhance decision-making;
Stay current with emerging AI technologies, tools, and best practices;
Contribute to the organisation’s digital innovation roadmap and AI strategy;
Work with cross-functional teams to understand business requirements and translate them into technical solutions;
Communicate technical concepts and model outputs to non-technical stakeholders;
Provide technical guidance and support to internal teams adopting AI solutions;
Ensure AI solutions comply with organisational governance, data privacy, and ethical standards;
Support the development of responsible and transparent AI practices;
Maintain documentation for AI models, processes, and system integrations;
Contribute to the internal knowledge base promoting the use, understanding, and application of AI tools and solutions;
Develop and co-create training materials, user guides, and documentation to support adoption and effective utilisation of AI systems;
Provide technical guidance and ongoing support to users to ensure effective and responsible use of AI solutions.
Grade 12 or Equivalent (Essential);
Bachelor’s Degree in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Data Science, Engineering, Mathematics, or a related field (Essential);
Postgraduate qualification (Advantageous);
2-5 years’ experience in software development and engineering (Essential);
Experience in AI Solutions and automations (Essential);
Knowledge of Software development;
Knowledge of Large Language Models;
Knowledge of API integration;
Knowledge of AI technologies, tools, models;
Interpersonal skills;
Attention to detail;
Results driven;
Able to handle sensitive and confidential information;
Ability to keep one’s composure in a fast moving, dynamic environment;
Strong Problem solving and decision-making skills;
Customer centricity.
Personal Attributes
Ability to work in a team and independently;
Internal and external networking;
Integrity and values;
Confidence.
Application Guideline
Email applications will not be accepted;
Preference will be given to members of under-represented designated groups;
Should no feedback be provided within two (2) weeks from the closing date, please consider your application as unsuccessful.
FlySafair Reserves The Right
Not to proceed with this vacancy;
To appoint the selected candidates based on its operational requirements.
Closing Date: 22 April 2026
